"""Nobel Prize in Physics, 1901-2026, one node per distinct prize citation.

Columns
  id          year plus a/b suffix when a year has two separately-cited contributions.
              2003 and 2016 are single citations split by laureate because the
              cited work spans decades (2003: Ginzburg-Landau/Abrikosov 1950-57
              vs Leggett 1975; 2016: Kosterlitz-Thouless 1972 vs TKNN/Haldane
              1982-88). Analyses count them as one prize.
  year        award year (the year the prize is "for"; e.g. Einstein = 1921)
  laureates   list of names
  motivation  official motivation text, transcribed from the Nobel Foundation record
  field       analysis field tag (ours, not Nobel's; Nobel's category is always Physics)
  kind        T = theory, E = experimental discovery, I = instrument / method / technology
  work_year   year of the key recognised work (first decisive publication/observation)

Provenance: motivations were transcribed, not downloaded. nobelprize.org and
api.nobelprize.org were unreachable from the build environment, so run
scripts/verify_against_api.py where those hosts are reachable to diff every
motivation against the official API before citing the text verbatim.
The 2026 entry was confirmed by web search on 2026-10-06 (announcement day).
"""

